# Navigation

## Expo Router Only
Use `router` from `expo-router` or `<Link />`. Do not use React Navigation APIs directly.

## Route Groups
| Group | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `(auth)` | Welcome, therapist login, patient join |
| `(onboarding)` | Device check, model download |
| `(app)` | Therapist core app: record, processing, preview, export |
| `(patient)` | Patient waiting room / join flow |

New group folders need `_layout.tsx` when they share header or tab state.

Role guards: `(app)` requires `session.role === 'therapist'`; `(patient)` requires `patient`. Unauthenticated users go to `/(auth)/welcome`. Demo auth details: `docs/UI_DUAL_AUTH_AND_MOTION.md`.

## Screen Structure
Screens are thin. Root with `ThemedView` or `SafeAreaView`:

```typescript
import { SafeAreaView } from 'react-native-safe-area-context';
import { ThemedText } from '@/components/themed-text';

export default function RecordScreen() {
  return (
    <SafeAreaView style={{ flex: 1 }}>
      <ThemedText type="title">Record</ThemedText>
    </SafeAreaView>
  );
}
```

## Paywall Gating
Trial-gated screens/actions must call `router.push('/paywall')` before access. Navigation enforces the gate — not conditional rendering alone.

## Deep Links
Use Expo Router file paths. Test on both iOS and Android when adding new routes.
